  "description": "EWUXEB crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C102 H201 Co2 Gd9 N4 O50 P4,12(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd7 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd8 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd9 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.042-3.892 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.31-110.13°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [CoIII2GdIII9(μ3-OH)2(tBuPO3)4(deaH)4(O2CtBu)13(HO2CtBu)]·12H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies Co(III), Gd(III).",
